<a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
</div>
<h2 id="rookie">A Rookie Year Cut Short</h2>
<p>Hunter, the No. 2 overall pick in the 2025 draft, was limited to seven games as a rookie after undergoing season-ending knee surgery to repair his LCL. In that short window he still caught 28 passes for 298 yards and a touchdown on offense, while adding 15 tackles and three passes defended on defense — a snapshot of the two-way workload the Jaguars intend to give him for a full season in 2026. Jacksonville coach Liam Coen has pushed back on any suggestion Hunter would be limited to one side of the ball going forward.</p>
